{"id": "EUVD-2026-108128", "enisaUuid": "829c8a03-a0f8-339a-bd8a-3ba1b32bafca", "description": "QloApps through 1.7.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in OrderDetailController::displayAjaxSubmitRefundRequest() that allows authenticated customers to submit refunds for other customers' service lines. Attackers can submit foreign id_service_product_order_detail values with their own id_order to create refund records, cancel victims' service lines, and corrupt refund quantities.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:44", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/pull/1930", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/commit/105241f9a77e94b30d6c2d577d14b247f33a5fba", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps/blob/v1.7.0/controllers/front/OrderDetailController.php#L624-L631", "https://github.com/Qloapps/QloApps", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/qloapps-through-1.7.0-idor-via-orderdetailcontroller-refund-request"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115326", "GHSA-7cwv-h2vr-67q3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "95254312-c0ee-35c2-b6f5-003bd78890ba", "product": {"name": "QloApps", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "92cbe096-f79a-3263-bd7a-565c4c94e10b", "vendor": {"name": "Webkul"}}], "isExploited": false}